--
-- Test Description:
-- TODO put some description here
--
-- Detailed Test Description
--  1. Initialise suitable wait states for the test.
--  2. Check reset values of registers and setup interrupts
--     and then enable receive in 100M mode into a 64-bit DMA data bus.
--  3. Send several IP frames with either SNAP or ethernet encapsulation, which
--     have good IP checksum but are not checked for TCP or UDP.
--
-- Test 1.1
--    This is a minimum size TCP frame
--      - Not a VLAN or SNAP packet
--      - No IP options
--      - No TCP options
--      - No actual packet data
--      = 54 bytes (not incl CRC)
-- Test 1.2
--    Broadcast frame, IP checksum correct, Min length IP, no IP options,
--    no TCP or UDP, with VLAN tag with no CFI bit.
--    The frame should be copied to memory, with status indicating IP header
--    checksum only check (bits [23:22] = 01) and no SNAP (bit 24 low).
-- Test 1.3
--    Broadcast frame, IP checksum correct, Min length IP, no IP options,
--    no TCP or UDP, with SNAP.
--    The frame should be copied to memory, with status indicating IP header
--    checksum only check (bits [23:22] = 01) and SNAP (bit 24 high).
-- Test 1.4
--    Broadcast frame, IP checksum correct, Min length IP, no IP options,
--    no TCP or UDP, with VLAN and SNAP.
--    The frame should be copied to memory, with status indicating IP header
--    checksum only check (bits [23:22] = 01) and SNAP (bit 24 high).
-- Test 1.5 
--    Broadcast frame, IP checksum correct, Min length IP, no IP options,
--    no TCP or UDP, with neither VLAN nor SNAP.
--    The frame should be copied to memory, with status indicating IP header
--    checksum only check (bits [23:22] = 01) and no SNAP (bit 24 low).
-- Test 1.6
--    Broadcast frame, IP Fragmentation (MF bit set), otherwise valid 
--    IP and TCP.
--    The frame should be copied to memory, with status indicating IP header
--    checksum only check (bits [23:22] = 01) and no SNAP (bit 24 low).
-- Test 1.7
--    Broadcast frame, IP Fragmentation (Fragment offset non zero), 
--    otherwise valid IP and TCP.
--    The frame should be copied to memory, with status indicating IP header
--    checksum only check (bits [23:22] = 01) and no SNAP (bit 24 low).
-- Test 1.8
--    Broadcast frame, IP checksum correct, Min length IP, IP options,
--    no TCP or UDP, with neither VLAN nor SNAP.
--    The frame should be copied to memory, with status indicating IP header
--    checksum only check (bits [23:22] = 01) and no SNAP (bit 24 low).
-- 
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

pinsc(50) loopback 0 half_duplex 1  extint 0 --  check reset state

-- check and initialise the relevant registers
apbrd(100) 00 00000000  -- check reset value of network control register
apbwr      28 ffffffff  -- enable all interrupts
apbwr      04 00280000  -- check reset value of network config register
apbrd      04 00280000  -- check reset value of network config register
apbrd      08 00000006  -- check reset value of network status register
apbwr      1c 55555500  -- write address of transmit buffer descriptor in memory
apbrd      1c 55555500  -- check transmit queue pointer
apbwr      10 00020c04  -- enable 4k ram and tcp offload
apbwr      00 00000208  -- write tx_go and enable tx


